  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Traversone. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Traversone (also Rovescino, CiapanÃ², Tressette a Perdere) is an Italian reverse trick-taking game where players try to AVOID taking point cards. It uses the Tressette ranking (3-2-A high) and scoring system, but the goal is inverted â€” whoever accumulates the MOST points loses. A 'Cappotto' (sweep) reverses the penalty to opponents.",
    objective: 'Avoid taking point cards. A player who reaches the agreed penalty total loses, unless taking all points by cappotto reverses the penalty.',
    gameplay: 'Players must follow suit if possible. There are no trumps; the highest card of the led suit wins the trick and leads next. Card points are counted as penalties instead of rewards.',
    keyRules: [
      'Uses Tressette ranking and no trump suit.',
      'Must follow suit when possible.',
      'Point cards captured in tricks are bad.',
      'A player who captures all available points makes cappotto and can reverse the penalty according to table rules.',
